-- title:
--   Roof generation for the Hecke exchange square
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N,\ell,\ell',M$ be nonzero natural numbers with $M = N\ell\ell'$. Assume `FunctionFieldGeneration M`: for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $M$ the Laurent series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,d\;j_q$, i.e. $j$ re-expanded in $q^{d}$, lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by $j_q$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,M\;j_q$. Assume further a datum `ModularPolynomialData ℓ'`, that is, a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[j][X]$ of degree $\psi(\ell') = \sum_{d \mid \ell',\ d \text{ squarefree}} \ell'/d$ which annihilates the pair $(j_q, j_{q^{\ell'}})$. Write $F^{\mathrm{full}}_n = \mathbb{Q}(\text{divisorExpansions } n) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ and let $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_n$ denote its base change `laurentBaseChange`, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F^{\mathrm{full}}_n$. From $M = N\ell\ell'$ one extracts the divisibilities $N\ell \mid M$ and $(N\ell')\ell \mid M$. The conclusion is that the $L$-subalgebra of $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$ generated by the union of the range of `towerSubstBar` on $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{N\ell'}$ (the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ followed by the inclusion into $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$) and the range of the inclusion `towerInclBar` of $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{N\ell}$ is all of $L \cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$.
--
--   This is the generation input to the exchange square relating the degeneracy and Hecke substitution maps at level $N$ for two primes $\ell,\ell'$ (including $\ell = \ell'$): the roof field at level $M = N\ell\ell'$ is generated by its two subfields coming from levels $N\ell'$ and $N\ell$. It is used in the identities for $\mathrm{heckeDivBar}$ with the Atkin–Lehner and Fricke involutions and in the diagonal identity for Hecke correspondences at a prime; no commutation statement is asserted here.
